## How I'd execute this in Copilot

Don't expect Copilot to produce a perfect 20-section architecture article in one shot. Use this sequence:

1. Repository discovery

   Ask Copilot to inspect all relevant repositories/files and produce an implementation inventory. Review whether it has identified the correct workflows, scripts and manifest.
2. Architecture reconstruction

   Ask it to trace the real workflow call chain and create the architecture and sequence diagrams. Correct any inaccurate arrows or missing components.
3. Manifest contract

   Ask it to document the actual YAML schema, field definitions, examples, validation rules and Vault mapping. This deserves its own review because it is the interface between application teams and the central platform.
4. Code-level documentation

   Ask it to generate snippets from actual source files, with file references and explanations. Do not accept invented or outdated snippets.
5. Final documentation review

   Ask it to verify every statement against source code, separate implemented controls from recommendations, and produce the final README.

